{"traceId":"hw-personalization-proof:decision:r10","eventType":"theory_decision","evidenceRead":["shared-baseline-session:baseline:completion","shared-quest-session:quest:completion","shared-baseline-session:baseline:completion:engagement","negative-uncertain:baseline:rating","shared-quest-session:quest:completion:engagement","negative-uncertain:quest:rating"],"theoryUsed":"personalization-proof-theory","changeSummary":"quest_evaluating -> boss_generating","reason":"Prediction called for ≥0.70 accuracy on fresh unassisted material; the Quest delivered 3/3 unseen, unassisted, independent-probe correct readings across equal groups, missing factor, and word-problem interpretation (accuracy 1.0), and the predicted factor-pair overgeneralization error never appeared. That supports transfer at the evidence limit of independent performance — it does not establish synthesis, since every Quest item still isolated one target at a time. Boss eligibility is met on fresh unassisted evidence, so the next instrument must force the three targets to collide inside one problem. The one loud counter-signal is engagement: both runs finalized at fun 1/5 with confusion and hesitation flagged and no replay requested, while accuracy stayed perfect. Correct answers plus no enjoyment reads as an instrument that was too thin and too talky for a 9-year-old who is clearly not being challenged, so the Boss escalates real difficulty and gives him something concrete to move and something real to lose.","writesTo":["/Users/jamaltaylor/Development/sunny-demo-main/outputs/math-personalization-live/2026-08-08T13-43-30/personalization/negative-uncertain/isolated-context/src/context/personalization-proof-child/homework/cycles/hw-personalization-proof.json"],"createdAt":"2026-08-08T19:10:33.622Z"}
